lopment district","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-09-21","sponsor":null,"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-11-03","text":"(LC) Draft Ready for Delivery","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-29","text":"(LC) Draft in Final Drafter Review","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-29","text":"(LC) Draft in Assembly","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-26","text":"(LC) Draft in Input/Proofing","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-22","text":"(LC) Draft in Edit","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-09-24","text":"(LC) Draft in Legal Review","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-09-21","text":"(LC) Drafter Assigned","chamber":null}],"law":null,"policyArea":"County Finance, Local Finance, Local Government","url":"https://bills.legmt.gov/#/lc/bill/3/LC0450","textUrl":"https://api.legmt.gov/docs/v1/documents/getContent?documentId=16742083","versions":[{"label":"LC0450.pdf","date":null,"url":"https://api.legmt.gov/docs/v1/documents/getContent?documentId=16742083","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would let a resort area district board create a targeted economic development district and use tax increment financing, which is a way to use future tax growth for project costs. It would require the board to get an infrastructure deficiency report and adopt a development plan that explains the needed fixes and how the money would be used. The rules would apply to resort area districts and would take effect when the act is approved.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MT-2027-LC399":{"id":"MT-2027-LC399","passed":false,"number":"LC 399","title":"Require only executive branch offices with essential election duties to be open on election day","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-09-19","sponsor":null,"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-11-03","text":"(LC) Draft Ready for Delivery","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-06","text":"(LC) Draft in Assembly","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-05","text":"(LC) Draft in Final Drafter Review","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-01","text":"(LC) Draft in Input/Proofing","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-09-29","text":"(LC) Draft in Edit","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-09-28","text":"(LC) Draft in Legal Review","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-09-19","text":"(LC) Drafter Assigned","chamber":null}],"law":null,"policyArea":"Elections, Public Officers and Employees","url":"https://bills.legmt.gov/#/lc/bill/3/LC0399","textUrl":"https://api.legmt.gov/docs/v1/documents/getContent?documentId=16599568","versions":[{"label":"LC0399.pdf","date":null,"url":"https://api.legmt.gov/docs/v1/documents/getContent?documentId=16599568","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would require only state executive branch offices with essential election duties to be open on state general election day. It would change the state rule on office hours for those offices and would take effect on July 1, 2027. It would also require the secretary of state to send a copy of the act to each federally recognized tribal government in Montana.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MT-2027-LC378":{"id":"MT-2027-LC378","passed":false,"number":"LC 378","title":"Allow water rights to certain subdivisions","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-09-17","sponsor":null,"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-11-03","text":"(LC) Draft Ready for Delivery","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-19","text":"(LC) Draft in Final Drafter Review","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-19","text":"(LC) Draft in Assembly","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"(LC) Draft in Input/Proofing","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-06","text":"(LC) Draft in Edit","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-09-30","text":"(LC) Draft in Legal Review","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-09-17","text":"(LC) Drafter Assigned","chamber":null}],"law":null,"policyArea":"Natural Resources, Property, Water","url":"https://bills.legmt.gov/#/lc/bill/3/LC0378","textUrl":"https://api.legmt.gov/docs/v1/documents/getContent?documentId=16607066","versions":[{"label":"LC0378.pdf","date":null,"url":"https://api.legmt.gov/docs/v1/documents/getContent?documentId=16607066","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would let some owners of recorded land tracts use a water-right permit exception if they got a state water letter before February 14, 2024, got subdivision approval when needed, and file a notice of completion by January 1, 2032. It would also update Montana water law to spell out when some groundwater uses do not need a permit and how notices and water-right certificates must be filed. The change would take effect right away.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MT-2027-LC240":{"id":"MT-2027-LC240","passed":false,"number":"LC 240","title":"Provide for Article V commissioner selection and oversight","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-09-15","sponsor":null,"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-11-03","text":"(LC) Draft in Assembly","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-26","text":"(LC) Draft in Final Drafter Review","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-22","text":"(LC) Draft in Input/Proofing","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-20","text":"(LC) Draft in Edit","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-10-19","text":"(LC) Draft in Legal Review","chamber":null},{"date":"2026-09-15","text":"(LC) Drafter Assigned","chamber":null}],"law":null,"policyArea":"Federal Government, Legislature","url":"https://bills.legmt.gov/#/lc/bill/3/LC0240","textUrl":"https://api.legmt.gov/docs/v1/documents/getContent?documentId=16744572","versions":[{"label":"LC0240.pdf","date":null,"url":"https://api.legmt.gov/docs/v1/documents/getContent?documentId=16744572","type":"PDF"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would set rules for choosing, overseeing, and removing Montana commissioners to an Article V convention called to propose U.S. constitutional amendments. It would require commissioners to meet set age, residency, voting, and conflict rules, follow limits in their commission, and take an oath. It would also create a legislative advisory committee to fill vacancies, monitor conduct, and help remove commissioners who go beyond their authority.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false}}}